  "claim": "The creator of The Life & Times of Tim and this Midwestern man are not both art dealers. The other man currently owns the Nathaniel L. McCready House.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Larry Gagosian. Sentence: Lawrence Gilbert \"Larry\" Gagosian (born April 19, 1945) is an Armenian American art dealer who owns the Gagosian Gallery chain of art galleries.\nPage: Steve Dildarian. Sentence: Steve Dildarian (born November 3, 1969) is an American former advertising copywriter who is the creator, writer, producer and voice of Tim in the HBO animated television series \"The Life & Times of Tim\" (2008-2012).\nPage: Nathaniel L. McCready House. Sentence: In 2011, the home was purchased by Larry Gagosian, who demolished the mansion's interior.\nPage: The Life &amp; Times of Tim. Sentence: The series was created by Steve Dildarian, and is about a hapless man in his mid-20s named Tim (voiced by Dildarian) who lives in New York City with his girlfriend Amy.",
