        "original_id": "11288ae1-1850-5c5b-a671-d66944cf383a",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Larry Gagosian, Steve Dildarian\n- Companies: Gagosian Gallery\n- TV Series: The Life & Times of Tim\n- Places: Nathaniel L. McCready House, New York City\n- Roles: art dealer, advertising copywriter, creator, writer, producer, voice actor\n\nFacts:\n- Larry Gagosian was born on April 19, 1945.\n- Larry Gagosian is an Armenian American art dealer who owns the Gagosian Gallery chain of art galleries.\n- Steve Dildarian was born on November 3, 1969.\n- Steve Dildarian is an American former advertising copywriter.\n- In 2008, HBO premiered The Life & Times of Tim, an animated television series created by Steve Dildarian.\n- Steve Dildarian was the creator, writer, producer, and voice of Tim in The Life & Times of Tim from 2008 to 2012.\n- The Life & Times of Tim is about Tim, a hapless man in his mid-20s who lives in New York City with his girlfriend Amy.\n- In The Life & Times of Tim, Steve Dildarian voiced the character Tim.\n- In 2011, Larry Gagosian purchased the Nathaniel L. McCready House.\n- In 2011, Larry Gagosian demolished the interior of the Nathaniel L. McCready House mansion.",
